WEBVTT

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.699
Layfon... Can he never return here?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.325
Leerin...

00:00:35.243 --> 00:00:37.245
I'm terribly sorry!

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:42.459
It is without doubt
that for him, this is home...

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:46.838
and that he is an important person to you.

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:48.381
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.967
It is not impossible for
him to be allowed return.

00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:53.053
But it would take some time.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:53.928
Then...

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:59.309
However, even if it could be so,
would he <i>wish </i>to return?

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:03.980
That is a problem that
must be solved, and not by me.

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:10.236
You Saiharden tend to leave our city, correct?

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.780
Yes, ma'am.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.867
Many of those who left to
follow the first-generation Salinban

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:20.080
were disciples of the Saiharden
two generations previous.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.917
Even your brother disciple joined
those who began calling themselves

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.670
the Salinban Mercenary Training Group.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.341
Ryuho Gaju.
A man whose skills far exceeded my own.

00:01:31.341 --> 00:01:36.054
By rights, he should have been
the successor to the Saiharden name.

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:37.514
He is dead.

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:38.932
It can't be!

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:44.938
"The Sentiment That Lies in the Barrel of a Gun"

00:01:58.034 --> 00:02:00.495
He fought against the
contaminoids, following which

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:05.375
he could not cleanse
the contamination that remained within.

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:06.543
I see...

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:11.297
The Saiharden martial family
is Glendan's precious treasure.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.968
Think only of passing on
your skills to the next generation.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.595
Leerin Marfes.

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:19.222
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:19.222 --> 00:02:22.434
As he is part of the Saiharden,

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:25.979
it cannot be denied that
leaving our city is in his nature.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:29.190
You should resign yourself to that fact.

00:02:34.904 --> 00:02:37.907
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:41.494
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:49.210
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:54.799
<i>Roaming around the city having lost my map</i>

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:58.094
<i>Even a dying world</i>

00:02:58.094 --> 00:03:04.893
<i>Let me hear a life deep</i>
<i>within that won't stop running</i>

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:07.896
<i>I seared the undying light into my eyes</i>

00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:11.441
<i>Refusing to shut them</i>
<i>even when they dried</i>

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:18.156
<i>I don't believe anything I can</i>
<i>obtain without getting hurt</i>

00:03:18.156 --> 00:03:24.371
<i>A single emotion</i>
<i>directed toward someone</i>

00:03:24.371 --> 00:03:31.628
<i>Splits the steel darkness</i>
<i>like the light of morning</i>

00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:36.216
<i>One day brave your</i>
<i>truth and brave yourself</i>

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:39.761
<i>So you will drastically change</i>

00:03:39.761 --> 00:03:45.600
<i>Compounded strength and prayers</i>

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.354
<i>Intersecting futures</i>
<i>and wishes held close</i>

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:52.941
<i>I will give these to no one</i>

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:54.442
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:03:54.442 --> 00:03:59.656
<i>It links our hearts</i>

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:09.374
Bein' unable to hide your
presence is bad news for a shooter.

00:04:09.374 --> 00:04:14.921
Try stalking a guy you like!
I'm tellin' you, it'll be good practice.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:17.340
I-I couldn't do that!

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.843
Who the hell are you two?

00:04:19.843 --> 00:04:22.262
This little spectacle
isn't the reason you're here.

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:27.225
You are correct.
Yours truly is named Haia Salinban Laia.

00:04:27.225 --> 00:04:29.561
The Salinban Mercenary Training Group, eh?

00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:33.023
I'm the third-generation leader.
And that's Myunfa.

00:04:33.023 --> 00:04:35.358
A pleasure to meet you.

00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:37.527
What are you doing in the academic city?

00:04:37.527 --> 00:04:41.698
I doubt you were asked
to instruct our Military Arts students.

00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:44.784
Unfortunately, I'm not here to ply my wares.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:49.456
I came all this way because I want your help.

00:04:49.456 --> 00:04:53.752
You're from a noble Glendan family,
so it wouldn't be odd if you knew...

00:04:53.752 --> 00:04:58.548
The secret origin of the
Salinban Mercenary Training Group, that is.

00:05:00.383 --> 00:05:03.470
That face tells me that you do.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.430
Gor, what's this about?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.640
Shante, you wait over there.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.559
Why?! No way!

00:05:09.559 --> 00:05:14.773
There's nothin' to hide.
We'll be sure to meet them soon...

00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:16.191
The Fallen Ones.

00:05:16.191 --> 00:05:20.487
I thought that was just idle talk.
Do they really exist?

00:05:20.487 --> 00:05:22.697
You are a doubter, aren't you?

00:05:22.697 --> 00:05:27.577
There was one. Not here,
but at the busted-up city a ways down.

00:05:27.577 --> 00:05:31.289
I checked it out but couldn't
find anything, so I came here.

00:05:31.289 --> 00:05:33.541
What are the "Fallen Ones"?

00:05:33.541 --> 00:05:35.460
To be high-falutin' about it,

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:39.214
they're the crazed power
spawned from wrecked cities.

00:05:39.214 --> 00:05:43.718
But to word it more appropriately,
they're the cities' spirits,

00:05:43.718 --> 00:05:48.431
living on though their cities are gone.

00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:52.644
The 17th Platoon's nen'i operator
may have noticed something.

00:05:52.644 --> 00:05:55.146
If you're tryin' to give me the runaround...

00:05:56.648 --> 00:06:00.485
And if the Fallen Ones
truly exist, then as a Lueckens,

00:06:00.485 --> 00:06:01.861
I cannot turn my back.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.488
I gotcha.

00:06:07.575 --> 00:06:13.289
All right then, Gorneo-<i>san</i>.
Who is this nen'i operator?

00:06:14.249 --> 00:06:17.419
Well, this is all smashed up...

00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:21.089
It'd be impossible to repair.
Making a new one would be faster.

00:06:21.089 --> 00:06:23.633
Sorry. And thank you.

00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:27.262
I still have the data,
so I can make one pretty quickly.

00:06:28.763 --> 00:06:31.266
Here. Try restoring this one.

00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:32.892
All right.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:36.938
Restoration.

00:06:39.357 --> 00:06:41.526
But... this is a single-edged blade.

00:06:41.526 --> 00:06:42.944
Yup.

00:06:43.987 --> 00:06:46.656
It hit me when I was watching you practice.

00:06:46.656 --> 00:06:49.075
Rather than a sword
that takes force to hack with,

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:51.870
you're more suited to a blade
that can cut and stab, right?

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.205
That's how you move.

00:06:54.456 --> 00:06:56.416
What? You don't like it?

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:59.336
It's not that. It's just...

00:07:01.004 --> 00:07:03.506
This should let you draw on more power.

00:07:03.506 --> 00:07:07.427
Why you'd back away from that, I don't know.

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:11.222
In that case, what's the power even for?

00:07:16.853 --> 00:07:18.855
What's it for...?

00:07:19.564 --> 00:07:20.982
What's wrong?

00:07:21.399 --> 00:07:24.194
<i>You </i>not noticing someone's presence?

00:07:24.194 --> 00:07:26.571
You have a fever? Still tired from yesterday?

00:07:26.571 --> 00:07:28.365
I-It's nothing!

00:07:28.365 --> 00:07:29.783
Hey!

00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:38.124
Circuit? So you're the
inspector that goes around cities?

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:42.087
I don't know. I've never seen one before.

00:07:42.504 --> 00:07:45.340
So, what do you want from me and Gedosh?

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:48.343
He accepted a plea bargain from me.

00:07:48.343 --> 00:07:52.138
We protect you and he gives us information...

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:56.434
Information about a person
who was connected to the Kolfe family.

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:59.354
Connected to the Kolfe family? Who is it?

00:07:59.354 --> 00:08:02.816
Gedosh is going to tell me that.
I want you to meet him now.

00:08:02.816 --> 00:08:04.567
Is that okay with you?

00:08:04.567 --> 00:08:08.238
Well, if it's gonna take a while,
I need to make a phone call.

00:08:08.238 --> 00:08:11.700
I need to call home, you know?
My daughter is waiting.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.661
And I need to tell my
mother I'll be home late, okay?

00:08:14.661 --> 00:08:17.455
I see. Use that phone there.

00:08:17.455 --> 00:08:19.082
Thank you.

00:08:24.754 --> 00:08:28.425
It's not "nothing" at all, is it?
Are you worried about something?

00:08:28.425 --> 00:08:29.968
It's really nothing...

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:31.469
What are you worrying about?

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:34.389
Why are you so preoccupied with this, ma'am?

00:08:34.389 --> 00:08:38.351
Well, that's obvious.
Because you're one of my men.

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:40.311
Yes, but still...

00:08:40.311 --> 00:08:42.522
So tell me what's up.

00:08:43.565 --> 00:08:44.899
Naruki?

00:08:44.899 --> 00:08:49.487
Is now a good time? I'm here
for my boss, to give you a message.

00:08:49.487 --> 00:08:51.865
What is the message?

00:08:51.865 --> 00:08:54.492
It's about all the commotion yesterday.

00:08:54.492 --> 00:08:57.328
The investigation of the Overload
smuggling ring is moving forward.

00:08:57.328 --> 00:08:59.873
He wants to know if we can ask for your help.

00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:03.835
Students are actually buying it? Ridiculous.

00:09:03.835 --> 00:09:07.589
Zuellni's students aren't
so careless as to dabble in that.

00:09:07.589 --> 00:09:09.966
I would like to think not,

00:09:09.966 --> 00:09:13.595
but given the situation,
with the military arts competition near

00:09:13.595 --> 00:09:17.057
and the platoon members
so fiercely devoted to their school...

00:09:17.057 --> 00:09:18.266
What proof do you have?

00:09:18.266 --> 00:09:23.146
Unless you agree to do this,
I can tell you no more.

00:09:23.146 --> 00:09:26.983
Then why did you let
me hear the name "Overload"?

00:09:26.983 --> 00:09:32.989
It's not just Layfon: you need
either my help or my consent. Why?

00:09:32.989 --> 00:09:37.369
Unless you agree, I can't tell you that either.

00:09:37.369 --> 00:09:39.079
The suspect...

00:09:39.079 --> 00:09:42.290
is someone close to us, isn't it?

00:09:44.459 --> 00:09:45.710
Is that all?

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.921
Huh? Uh, yes.

00:09:47.921 --> 00:09:49.964
Let me repeat this...

00:09:49.964 --> 00:09:53.843
Fon-Fon, you've been recruited
to help the municipal police,

00:09:53.843 --> 00:09:55.845
so this week's practice has been canceled.

00:09:55.845 --> 00:09:57.263
Yes.

00:09:57.889 --> 00:09:59.516
Understood.

00:10:02.936 --> 00:10:05.897
Sen... Felli!

00:10:15.073 --> 00:10:21.371
Hiding things! Keeping secrets!
<i>You</i>, Fon-Fon?!

00:10:21.371 --> 00:10:23.707
Um, hello.

00:10:23.707 --> 00:10:24.791
Who are you?

00:10:24.791 --> 00:10:27.544
Man, you sure kept us waitin'.

00:10:27.544 --> 00:10:28.962
Restoration!

00:10:30.005 --> 00:10:32.090
Brgh grnh bgr grhing!

00:10:33.967 --> 00:10:36.177
We won't do anything.

00:10:36.177 --> 00:10:40.140
That's like a suspicious character saying
"There's nothing suspicious about me."

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.976
Y'know, yours truly doesn't go for your type.

00:10:42.976 --> 00:10:46.396
Similarly, I would not wish to be liked by you.

00:10:47.856 --> 00:10:49.357
Felli!

00:10:49.691 --> 00:10:52.902
Ah! The gang's finally all here.

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:58.324
Felli-<i>chan</i>, you're just in time.

00:11:03.371 --> 00:11:06.041
Who are these people?

00:11:17.177 --> 00:11:20.889
Your rear defense is too slow!

00:11:20.889 --> 00:11:23.141
Siena! Keep your spear steady!

00:11:23.141 --> 00:11:26.311
Our suspects are Dinn Dee and the 10th Platoon.

00:11:26.311 --> 00:11:29.189
The boss would like you to catch them

00:11:29.189 --> 00:11:32.359
either in possession of
or actually using Overload.

00:11:32.359 --> 00:11:34.402
It can't be! Dinn Dee?

00:11:34.402 --> 00:11:37.447
But it wouldn't be out of self-interest...

00:11:37.447 --> 00:11:40.617
It would be out of a desire
to protect the city, right?

00:11:40.617 --> 00:11:44.829
Even so, that doesn't mean
we can accept the use of Overload.

00:11:45.663 --> 00:11:49.376
Sacrificing yourself to save something...

00:11:49.376 --> 00:11:53.797
It makes a lovely allegory,
but it's self-serving.

00:11:53.797 --> 00:11:56.633
It's simply running away from hardship.

00:11:56.633 --> 00:11:58.468
If it were me...

00:11:58.635 --> 00:12:03.598
If it were me, I'd protect
<i>everything</i>, including myself.

00:12:29.833 --> 00:12:31.251
Dinn.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:43.680
Don't make that face.
You're our platoon's good luck charm, Siena.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.933
You have to be as dauntless as ever.

00:12:48.143 --> 00:12:51.980
Don't worry. We're sure to win.

00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:54.399
See ya.

00:13:08.496 --> 00:13:10.123
Dinn.

00:13:13.084 --> 00:13:15.295
I need to talk to you.

00:13:17.088 --> 00:13:20.467
I have nothing to say.
Nor is it worth listening.

00:13:20.467 --> 00:13:22.093
It's important.

00:13:22.093 --> 00:13:24.220
Stop with the Overload.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.680
What are you talking about?

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:27.932
The municipal police have their eyes on you all.

00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:31.353
But you can still make it.
Get out of this while you can.

00:13:31.353 --> 00:13:33.396
You've got some nerve, talking like that.

00:13:33.396 --> 00:13:35.774
So now you're treating me like a criminal?

00:13:35.774 --> 00:13:39.736
It will be too late once they've found evidence.

00:13:39.736 --> 00:13:41.946
And if I stopped, then what?

00:13:41.946 --> 00:13:44.866
Why go this far, destroying yourself?

00:13:44.866 --> 00:13:47.535
I have to, to protect us.

00:13:47.535 --> 00:13:50.663
To beat the 1st Platoon, which the head
of the Military Arts Department leads.

00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:53.750
In competitions and in our overall grades...

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:56.878
For my plan to work at the competition,

00:13:56.878 --> 00:13:59.798
our achievements will have
to beat those of the 1st Platoon.

00:13:59.798 --> 00:14:00.757
Wait.

00:14:00.757 --> 00:14:04.344
Never mind grades:
If your plan could really work,

00:14:04.344 --> 00:14:05.887
you should be able to get support.

00:14:05.887 --> 00:14:07.305
Don't be naïve!

00:14:07.305 --> 00:14:11.476
It's <i>not </i>naïve. If you've
raised your abilities unfairly,

00:14:11.476 --> 00:14:14.479
how will you prove the validity of your plan?

00:14:14.479 --> 00:14:19.442
You all destroyed my ideals,
so shut the hell up about validity!

00:14:19.442 --> 00:14:22.612
You use dirty tricks to steal Sharnid from us,

00:14:22.612 --> 00:14:25.865
and now you lecture me
about right and wrong? <i>Me</i>?!

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.953
If you want to tell the police
about me, knock yourself out.

00:14:29.953 --> 00:14:32.664
I'm determined to do this,
with everything I've got.

00:14:32.664 --> 00:14:37.585
The one who protects Zuellni,
this city, will be <i>me</i>!

00:14:38.753 --> 00:14:45.510
And tell Sharnid: We can make
good on that promise, even without you!

00:15:04.738 --> 00:15:07.365
So, has there been any progress?

00:15:07.365 --> 00:15:09.701
No. Nothing yet.

00:15:10.994 --> 00:15:14.122
They won't show their true colors so easily.

00:15:14.122 --> 00:15:16.958
Naruki Gelni! Wait!

00:15:21.296 --> 00:15:24.257
I'm sorry. I approached Dinn.

00:15:24.674 --> 00:15:28.345
I wanted to do things properly,
my way. Please understand.

00:15:28.345 --> 00:15:30.263
What were you thinking?!

00:15:30.263 --> 00:15:33.683
Your "way"? What does that even matter?!

00:15:33.683 --> 00:15:36.853
You simply gave him information,
a way to get away with this!

00:15:36.853 --> 00:15:42.067
Please wait. I <i>had </i>to meet
Dinn and talk with him.

00:15:42.067 --> 00:15:45.945
Because there's a past to
Dinn and the Overload.

00:15:45.945 --> 00:15:47.781
A past?

00:15:47.781 --> 00:15:50.408
Is this about Senior Sharnid?

00:15:51.618 --> 00:15:54.662
It was before I'd formed the 17th Platoon

00:15:54.662 --> 00:15:57.665
and was assigned to another.

00:16:01.836 --> 00:16:05.340
They were overwhelmingly powerful,
right from their first battle.

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:08.343
Though third-year students,
they dominated their upperclassmen.

00:16:08.343 --> 00:16:12.347
To us, they were the symbols of a new era.

00:16:12.347 --> 00:16:14.683
They shone so brightly.

00:16:15.058 --> 00:16:16.476
But...

00:16:17.936 --> 00:16:22.065
Sharnid left the platoon
in the middle of a tournament.

00:16:22.065 --> 00:16:26.736
That broke up the trio that'd sustained
the platoon, and it crumbled.

00:16:26.736 --> 00:16:29.322
Dinn was absolutely furious...

00:16:29.322 --> 00:16:32.742
Furious enough to challenge Sharnid to a duel.

00:16:33.118 --> 00:16:35.286
Sharnid didn't put up a fight.

00:16:35.286 --> 00:16:38.248
He didn't hit Dinn once in return.

00:16:38.832 --> 00:16:39.833
Jeez...

00:16:39.833 --> 00:16:40.750
No way!

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:43.378
C'mon, where's the harm?

00:16:49.509 --> 00:16:53.513
I went and talked to Sharnid soon afterward.

00:16:53.513 --> 00:16:57.392
"I want to form a platoon. Join me."

00:16:58.643 --> 00:17:02.605
It's as if I stole Sharnid
from the 10th Platoon.

00:17:02.605 --> 00:17:04.232
But that's not the case, is it?

00:17:04.232 --> 00:17:07.694
Factually, no, but the platoon
members feel otherwise.

00:17:07.694 --> 00:17:11.698
What's more,
our 17th Platoon has gotten stronger...

00:17:11.698 --> 00:17:15.493
Strong enough to frighten the 10th.

00:17:21.332 --> 00:17:25.295
Dinn's "past" notwithstanding,
I have to report this to my boss.

00:17:25.295 --> 00:17:26.921
I know.

00:17:31.509 --> 00:17:32.927
Hey!

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:38.016
I ran into Felli-<i>chan </i>just now.
She said she can't make it today.

00:17:39.225 --> 00:17:40.643
What's with that?

00:17:40.643 --> 00:17:43.688
Just wanted to say, don't try so hard.

00:17:43.688 --> 00:17:44.731
Meaning what?

00:17:44.731 --> 00:17:49.402
About Dinn. If the municipal cops
are showing up in person,

00:17:49.402 --> 00:17:52.739
it means they're close
to nabbing their culprits, right?

00:17:52.739 --> 00:17:55.492
You... knew about this?

00:17:55.492 --> 00:17:59.287
No one knows their true powers better than me.

00:17:59.287 --> 00:18:03.792
There's no way someone's
kei could suddenly increase like that.

00:18:04.209 --> 00:18:05.627
Right?

00:18:09.673 --> 00:18:14.010
The upperclassmen will probably
denounce the Military Arts Department.

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:17.722
Vanzeh could even be let go as
head of the Military Arts Department

00:18:17.722 --> 00:18:20.433
to placate the student federation.

00:18:20.433 --> 00:18:22.977
The military arts competition
looks bleak for us.

00:18:22.977 --> 00:18:25.939
No... What about Zuellni?

00:18:25.939 --> 00:18:29.401
If they graduate before it happens,
then who cares, right?

00:18:29.401 --> 00:18:33.697
With things like this, there's only
one person we can go to for advice.

00:18:34.948 --> 00:18:36.783
Our Mr. Kalian.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.661
Are you sure we should?

00:18:40.245 --> 00:18:45.667
It can't be helped.
That's how far these guys have decided to go.

00:18:51.798 --> 00:18:54.676
And? What do you wish me to do?

00:18:54.676 --> 00:18:58.972
Sir, at this stage, I'm sure
you don't wish for any problems either.

00:18:58.972 --> 00:19:00.890
We'd like you to deal
with this matter privately.

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:04.436
"Dealing with it privately" is simple.

00:19:04.436 --> 00:19:08.231
I'll convince the chief of police
to close the investigation.

00:19:08.231 --> 00:19:09.941
But that won't...

00:19:09.941 --> 00:19:14.946
Of course, it will not be enough.
I will have you all act as well.

00:19:14.946 --> 00:19:16.781
And do what?

00:19:17.657 --> 00:19:21.619
You will soon face them in the competition, yes?

00:19:22.037 --> 00:19:24.205
You're telling us to destroy them?

00:19:24.205 --> 00:19:26.916
No, I don't wish you to go that far.

00:19:26.916 --> 00:19:29.919
Simply make them become
incapable of remaining a platoon.

00:19:29.919 --> 00:19:31.963
In which case, I could use my authority

00:19:31.963 --> 00:19:35.175
to order them to disband.

00:19:35.175 --> 00:19:37.177
Rob military artists of their military arts?

00:19:37.177 --> 00:19:40.597
Then shall the students be robbed of their city?

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:45.226
Can you do it, Layfon-<i>kun</i>?

00:19:48.396 --> 00:19:51.191
Layfon, if you can't do it, just say you can't.

00:19:51.191 --> 00:19:53.026
Oh, he can do it.

00:19:54.569 --> 00:19:55.362
Haia!

00:19:55.362 --> 00:19:58.114
What makes you think he can, Haia-<i>kun</i>?

00:19:58.114 --> 00:20:01.910
'Cause the Saiharden style
has that kinda technique.

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:03.745
Puncturing someone
with a "needle" of Ballistic Kei

00:20:03.745 --> 00:20:07.374
makes it easy to heal or break someone.

00:20:07.374 --> 00:20:11.753
Especially for a guy who used
to be a Keeper of the Heaven's Blade.

00:20:11.753 --> 00:20:15.090
Still, Saiharden techniques
take a single-edged blade.

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:18.176
They're impossible with a dual-edged sword.

00:20:18.551 --> 00:20:20.553
Put conversely,

00:20:20.553 --> 00:20:23.640
they <i>would </i>be possible
with a single-edged blade?

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:28.478
Sir, he is the leader of the
Salinban Mercenary Training Group,

00:20:28.478 --> 00:20:31.731
but we suspect he's involved with
the secret Overload ring.

00:20:31.731 --> 00:20:34.484
That's exactly what you yahoos

00:20:34.484 --> 00:20:38.488
got together and came here to cover up, right?

00:20:38.905 --> 00:20:39.906
Stop it!

00:20:39.906 --> 00:20:41.533
Fon-Fon!

00:20:43.159 --> 00:20:44.994
I won't pull any punches next time.

00:20:44.994 --> 00:20:48.289
Fine. I don't want you using the Saiharden name

00:20:48.289 --> 00:20:50.875
if you can't even use a single-edged blade.

00:20:50.875 --> 00:20:52.293
That is enough!

00:20:52.293 --> 00:20:56.923
Haia-<i>kun</i>. I called you because
you said you had words for Layfon-<i>kun</i>.

00:20:56.923 --> 00:20:58.717
Not to allow you to fight.

00:20:58.717 --> 00:21:00.343
"Words"?

00:21:01.094 --> 00:21:02.971
The Fallen Ones.

00:21:02.971 --> 00:21:06.391
You must've seen one,
in that ruined city over a ways.

00:21:06.391 --> 00:21:11.396
A weird creature that goes
against all common sense...

00:21:12.564 --> 00:21:15.942
It would be dangerous if that thing were here.

00:21:16.317 --> 00:21:19.320
That's why I'm gonna collect it.

00:21:23.575 --> 00:21:25.076
What is it, Nakki?

00:21:25.076 --> 00:21:26.953
Oh. Sorry, May.

00:21:26.953 --> 00:21:30.749
I'm just mad because work
has suddenly been put on hold.

00:21:30.749 --> 00:21:32.125
On hold?

00:21:32.125 --> 00:21:34.544
Oh. Yeah, it's nothing.

00:21:37.964 --> 00:21:40.759
Work on the mine will soon conclude.

00:21:40.759 --> 00:21:44.554
We may proceed with the platoon
battles as scheduled, yes?

00:21:58.068 --> 00:21:59.694
Now, now...

00:22:20.090 --> 00:22:22.092
I've got a favor to ask.

00:22:26.262 --> 00:22:36.356
<i>Hello, who are you thinking of?</i>

00:22:36.356 --> 00:22:43.446
<i>This letter still lies within my breast</i>

00:22:43.446 --> 00:22:53.498
<i>That fragment of memories</i>
<i>of you, suddenly encountered,</i>

00:22:53.498 --> 00:23:00.588
<i>has pierced my heart and I can't move</i>

00:23:00.588 --> 00:23:05.427
<i>I want you to notice, don't notice</i>

00:23:05.427 --> 00:23:09.139
<i>Do you treat me coldly because of love?</i>

00:23:09.139 --> 00:23:18.732
<i>I want to tell you "Be by my side," </i>
<i>but I can't say it</i>

00:23:19.524 --> 00:23:28.116
<i>It was in this filthy world</i>
<i>that I was able to meet you</i>

00:23:28.116 --> 00:23:39.294
<i>Please play this miracle</i>
<i>that has descended to my heart</i>

00:23:39.294 --> 00:23:47.302
<i>Zuellni my love</i>

00:23:53.975 --> 00:23:57.145
<i>The competition against the</i>
<i>10th Platoon has finally arrived.</i>

00:23:57.145 --> 00:24:01.024
<i>Dinn, though backed into a corner,</i>
<i>will not bend from his convictions.</i>

00:24:01.024 --> 00:24:04.444
<i>But in the background,</i>
<i>an unsettling shadow creeps forward...</i>

00:24:04.444 --> 00:24:06.488
<i>Next time, "The Fallen Ones Appear," and...</i>

00:24:06.488 --> 00:24:08.086
<i>Restoration!</i>
